// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// machinedpens — COLLECTION view  ·  PASTABLE ERD  ·  BUYER-FACING
//
// This file IS the paste. Copy with:
//   pbcopy < docs/data-model/collection.eraser
//
// Answers: "What do I own, and what's loaded in it right now?"
// 10 entities · 12 relationship lines. The full model is 20 / 37.
//   The open_5_carry_log shell is GONE — 5.5 answered it.
//
// ⚠️ LABELS, NOT SCHEMA. Identifiers here are the buyer-facing names from
//    docs/data-model/MODEL.md section 7b. The source of truth is
//    docs/data-model/MODEL.md; its structural expression is unchanged and
//    lives in docs/data-model/schema.eraser.
//
// ⚠️ DIRECTION CHANGE 2026-08-13 — field-log is DROPPED (already gone from
//    apps/ on origin/main) and there is NO app integration. This is no
//    longer "Brownie's layer": it is a LIMITED, web-only save.
//    5.3a ANSWERED — a saved config is A PEN YOU OWN: a finish, a pen tip,
//    and what is loaded. NOT a wishlist, and NOT an inventory: no price,
//    no serial, no condition. Those belonged to the app being dropped.
//    5.3b(i) ANSWERED (c), 2026-08-14 — a saved pen names the refill MODEL
//    (always) and the EXACT ONE (optional). R-A found all three makers
//    publish a complete size x colour matrix, so the exact one is usually
//    knowable; but nothing forces that catalogue to be filled, and the code
//    on the refill in your pen names the SIZE, so neither grain alone works.
//    5.3b(ii) ANSWERED (a), 2026-08-14 — NOTHING MORE, AND LESS ENTRY. No
//    nickname, no note, no new columns. This row stores ZERO specs already,
//    so they read through to the catalog; what changed is that the four
//    links arrive PRE-FILLED from the stock config. You type "copper
//    TiBolt" and correct whatever is wrong. Fill what the catalog makes
//    unambiguous, ask only where it branches — and the values are SAVED to
//    your row, so a later catalog edit never rewrites the pen you own.
//    5.4 ANSWERED, 2026-08-14 — own two of the same pen and they are TWO
//    ROWS, never a count. What tells them apart is usually the finish or a
//    small part, not the refill, so + `part_fitted`. No nickname.
//    5.5 ANSWERED, 2026-08-14 — A FIELD, NOT A LOG. "Log from day one" was
//    field-log's OWN premise and field-log is dropped. BVG: "we are just
//    recording things owned — the actual refill is trivial at this point,
//    it's more about the actual PEN AND PARTS." Knowing what was loaded
//    when someone said it fits is what a REPORT is for, and that is
//    append-only already. THE COLLECTION LAYER IS NOW COMPLETE.
//
// Rename map applied here (internal > buyer-facing):
//   collection_item > my_pen · product_variant > pen_finish
//   refill_variant > refill_option
//   product > pen · tip_option > tip (shortened, NOT renamed) · one_off > one_of_a_kind
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

title machinedpens — buyer view — my collection
notation crows-feet
typeface clean
styleMode plain

// ── WHAT I OWN ──────────────────────────────────────

my_pen [icon: package, color: gray] {
  id bigint pk
  owner_id bigint fk         // 5.3a — a pen YOU OWN has to name you.
                                 //   The committed users table (Clerk).
  pen_finish_id bigint fk    // points at the FINISH, not the pen —
                                 //   what you own is a specific object
  tip_id bigint fk              // which front end is fitted
  installed_refill_id bigint fk null // 5.3b(i) — WHICH REFILL. "An EnerGel
                                 //   LR7." Always recordable, even for a
                                 //   colour nobody has catalogued yet, and
                                 //   it is what every read path uses.
  installed_refill_option_id bigint fk null // 5.3b(i) — EXACTLY WHICH ONE.
                                 //   Optional: the size and colour you
                                 //   actually loaded. Fill it when you know
                                 //   it, skip it when you don't — the two
                                 //   can never contradict each other.
                                 //   ONE PICKER, not two: choosing the exact
                                 //   one fills the line above for you.
                                 // 5.5 — A FIELD, not a log. Swap the
                                 //   refill and this row updates.
                                 // 🔑 THIS IS THE REPORT ENTRY POINT.
                                 //   A report must name a specific pen
                                 //   tip (4.1) — a saved setup already
                                 //   does. "Pick your setup, tell us if
                                 //   it fits."
                                 // 5.4 — two of the same pen are TWO ROWS.
                                 // OPEN 5.x — owner-commissioned
                                 //   finishing: you send YOUR pen to
                                 //   KVR. Same fact, different side.
}

// ── WHAT IT IS (full form in the catalog view) ──────

pen_finish [icon: droplet, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk
  pen_id bigint fk
  material_id bigint fk null // C2 — points at the shared alloy
                          //   list, declared in the catalog view
  finish text null        // Machined | Stonewashed | DLC
  name text null          // "Golden Dragon"
  one_of_a_kind bool      // "no two will be exactly alike"
}

pen [icon: pen-tool, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk
  maker_id bigint fk
  slug text unique
  name text
  advance_mechanism enum  // JetPens' own facet: "LEAD ADVANCE MECHANISM"
  control enum            // what you operate — kept separate on purpose
}

tip [icon: git-merge, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk            // shortened from tip_option; schema name UNCHANGED
  pen_id bigint fk
  name text
}

refill [icon: edit-3, color: green] {
  id bigint pk
  brand text
  model text
  ink_or_lead enum        // ballpoint|gel|hybrid|rollerball|pressurized|
                          //   graphite|permanent_marker|highlighter
                          // NO tip_size, NO ink_colour — 5.2, 2026-08-14.
                          //   They moved to refill_option, because `refill`
                          //   is now the MODEL.
                          // ✅ 5.3b(i) ANSWERED (c) — my_pen points at BOTH:
                          //   HERE for "an EnerGel LR7", and at refill_option
                          //   for "the 0.7, Navy Blue" when you know it.
}

refill_option [icon: layers, color: green] {
  id bigint pk            // was refill_variant — 5.2. WHICH ONE YOU BUY.
  refill_id bigint fk     //   Shown here because 5.3b(i) lets a saved pen
  tip_size decimal null   //   name the exact one. Full form is in the
  ink_colour text null    //   catalog view.
}

part_fitted {
  my_pen_id bigint fk     // 5.4 — WHICH PARTS ARE ON YOUR PEN. The bronze
  part_id bigint fk       //   clip, the copper back piece. Tactile Turn
                          //   sells those alone in Titanium, Copper, Bronze
                          //   and Zirconium and says to MIX AND MATCH — you
                          //   only have to match the pen size.
                          // LOOKS, NOT FITS. A spring or a spacer is not a
                          //   choice you made: the refill dictated it, and
                          //   it already lives with the fit check. If you
                          //   fitted one nobody has recorded, that is a
                          //   REPORT, not a checkbox.
}

part [icon: tool] {
  id bigint pk            // full form in the compatibility view
  maker_id bigint fk null // null = generic / third-party
  kind enum               // clip|bolt|bolt_handle|top_cap|spring|o_ring|
                          //   spacer|adapter — the first four are yours to
                          //   choose, the rest come from the fit
  name text
}

maker [icon: factory] {
  id bigint pk
  name text
}

owner [icon: user] {
  id bigint pk            // the committed users table — Clerk-backed and
  clerk_id text unique    //   deliberately minimal. Never shown to anyone
}                         //   but you.


// ── RELATIONSHIPS ───────────────────────────────────

my_pen.owner_id > owner.id
my_pen.pen_finish_id > pen_finish.id
my_pen.tip_id > tip.id
my_pen.installed_refill_id > refill.id
my_pen.installed_refill_option_id > refill_option.id

refill_option.refill_id > refill.id

part_fitted.my_pen_id > my_pen.id
part_fitted.part_id > part.id
part.maker_id > maker.id

pen_finish.pen_id > pen.id
tip.pen_id > pen.id
pen.maker_id > maker.id

// ── ⚠️ TWO RULES THAT GOVERN THIS LAYER AND ARE INVISIBLE IN BOXES ──
//
// 1. THE COMPLETENESS GATE. You cannot own what the catalog does not fully
//    have. It needs no column — the required links above already say it:
//    a pen is ownable only when it has a MAKER, a PEN, a FINISH, a PEN TIP,
//    and that pen tip declares a REFILL STYLE. A pen we lack routes to a
//    SUBMISSION (you send us the details, we approve or amend, it goes
//    public, and then anyone can customize from it). That path is real and
//    is deliberately NOT modelled here yet — when it is built it should
//    reuse the report's shape: pending / approved / rejected, rejected rows
//    kept.
//
// 2. THE CATALOG FILLS THE ROW; YOU CORRECT IT. Type "copper TiBolt" and
//    every link above arrives PRE-FILLED from the stock configuration. Fill
//    what the catalog makes unambiguous, ASK ONLY WHERE IT BRANCHES — one
//    pen tip, fill it; more than one, ask once. "Copper TiBolt" branches:
//    the Full Size TiBolt takes a Schmidt, the G2 TiBolt takes a G2 Mini.
//    ⚠️ THE VALUES ARE WRITTEN TO YOUR ROW, not resolved on read — otherwise
//    the day a curator corrects what a pen ships with, every saved pen
//    silently changes what is loaded in it. A pen you own is not curated
//    state.
//
// ── ⚠️ WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT ──────────────────
//
// This layer was settled in five questions and gained TWO things. Everything
// else was answered by DELETING a question, so the absences are decisions:
//
//   drop number · serial · acquisition date · price paid · current value ·
//   condition · photos
//                  -> COLLECTOR INVENTORY. A saved pen is a pen you own, not
//                     a valuation. That shape belonged to an app that was
//                     dropped.
//   a nickname     -> the row already renders a name it does not store
//                     (maker + pen + finish + pen tip + what's loaded), and
//                     part_fitted now tells two copies apart. One nullable
//                     column away if the UI ever wants it.
//   a note         -> "this one rattles" / "I trimmed it 2 mm" are facts
//                     about a PAIRING, and the report already has a home for
//                     them where a curator can promote them into a fit check.
//                     A note here is where that knowledge goes to die.
//   a quantity     -> own two and they are TWO ROWS. A count cannot say which
//                     refill is in the second one, and cannot be the subject
//                     of a report.
//   a carry log    -> "log from day one" was the dropped app's own premise.
//                     What was loaded WHEN SOMEONE SAID IT FITS is the
//                     report, which is append-only already. A pen you own is
//                     state you EDIT.
//   functional parts in part_fitted
//                  -> a spring or a spacer is not a choice you made: the
//                     refill dictated it, and it already lives with the fit
//                     check. Only parts that change how the pen LOOKS belong
//                     here.
//
// 🔑 AND THIS IS THE REPORT ENTRY POINT. A report must name a specific pen
//    tip; a saved pen already does. "Pick your setup, tell us if it fits."
//    The moat gets what it asked for from the feature being kept.
